WEBVTT

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:05.690
In Kyoto there is a secret society
 that has existed since the Taisho era.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:09.150
There are always seven seats,

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:14.010
and the humans who occupy them are each 
called by the name of one of the Seven Lucky Gods.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:20.210
They are our natural enemies, who paralyze children with fear, the Friday Fellows.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.490
Why are they our natural enemies?

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.880
Because they eat tanuki 
hot pot at their year-end bash.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.130
In the course of our tranquil daily life,

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.410
it's a regularly scheduled nightmare we have once a year.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.380
Our dad, too, the great Shimogamo Soichiro,

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:43.020
met his end all too soon
 as a Friday Fellows hot pot.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.080
Thus we are reminded

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:51.100
that the ones on top of 
the food chain are the humans.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.990
<b>Episode Five: 
The Friday Fellows</b>

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.390
So you're still alive!

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.940
As you can see.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.580
From the look of it, 
you're still on the run?

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.780
I'm helping out at a secondhand camera 
shop in Osaka's Nipponbashi district.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:41.410
Are you going to be okay? 
Benten goes to hang out in Osaka, too.

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:43.080
Just don't tell her!

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.960
You think I can guarantee that?

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.600
When I'm threatened I 
rattle on without meaning to...

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.400
Is she gone?

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:03.740
Yeah.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:08.500
There<i> is</i> something 
irresistible about this thrill.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.110
Well then.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:25.390
About Benten,

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:30.580
Yaichiro went to ask 
Prof. Akadama to intercede,

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.190
but he came back fuming,

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:37.180
saying, "I'm over bowing
 my head to the professor!"

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.360
He was bristling mad!

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.680
He needs to learn to 
have a bit more tolerance.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:51.410
Even without his help, you never know, it 
might already be water under the bridge.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:56.020
That might be so, but Benten
 is such a dangerous person.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:58.530
So fickle and capricious.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:01.810
What'll you do if it's <i>not</i> 
water under the bridge?

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.010
I like you so much I want to eat you up.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:12.770
Ugh, humans are even nastier than tengu.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:16.400
But, you know, most of them are good people.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.250
You can say that because
 you owe your life to one.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:26.510
Your being brought into the world
 is also thanks to Mr. Yodogawa.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:31.410
I still remember the taste of 
the onigiri he gave me that time.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.330
We gotta be thankful.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.290
<b>Mamiana Antiques</b>

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.040
Man, I demolished that.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.320
You eat like a pig!

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.690
Kaisei?

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.280
Why are you in that chest?

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.340
Shut up! Who cares?

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:27.030
So, what's up lately?

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.840
Is Yajiro doing okay?

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:33.000
Yeah, he's doing fine at 
the bottom of his well.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:35.320
And he's doing personal affairs consulting.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:40.860
I... like Yajiro. I go for 
advice sometimes, too.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:46.420
There's also a rumor that Benten visits him.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:51.210
With her unrivaled invincibility 
what kind of worries could Benten have?

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:52.700
Like I would know!

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:58.000
It must be that she can't decide which 
tanuki to eat at the next year-end bash.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:02.920
There's a rumor you'll be boiled
 in a hot pot this year... Will you?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.670
Not planning on it.

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:08.960
This is all because you got involved with 
that half-baked tengu -- you're only a tanuki!

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:12.090
Go back to Osaka early.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:15.910
If you hang around too much, 
you'll really end up getting eaten.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:19.990
Living as a tanuki, there is always the 
chance one will be made into hot pot.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:24.140
When the time comes, 
I'm prepared to go laughing.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:26.950
You put up a bold front 
for a guy with no balls!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:34.480
It'll be an issue if I get caught, 
so hang onto this for me.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:37.200
What, a keepsake?

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:41.170
Tengu tobacco. Please
 get it to Prof. Akadama.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:46.200
While I'm away from Kyoto 
I left Yashiro to take care of him,

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:50.370
but the professor is giving him a hard time 
with all kinds of unreasonable demands.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:56.150
Sticking tengu tobacco in 
his mouth should shut him up.

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:58.180
This is no good. I can't see.

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:03.360
It's because you're in that 
chest. Just come out already.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.250
No way. I refuse.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.330
I don't get it. What are 
you saying I should do?

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.160
To the valued customer on the second floor,

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.920
Benten has arrived.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.740
Is that Yasaburo character here?

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:59.670
Well, he's called "Yasaburo the Fugitive,"

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.480
so he might have already run away.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:06.960
What would you like to do? 
I can take you to the Friday Fellows.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.510
I'm a little tired. I'll take a rest here.

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:14.970
Hey, Teikinbo.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:20.970
There are two Darumas 
here. Isn't that strange?

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:26.480
They're both burned in the same spot and 
they're dirty in the exact same way.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:30.530
I see. That certainly is mysterious.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:35.270
Yasaburo has always 
been good at shape-shifting.

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:52.790
Long time no see, Yasaburo.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:56.050
How did you know I was here?

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:59.560
I got a tip from Kinkaku and Ginkaku

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:04.200
that lately their little sister has 
been going out alone sometimes,

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:09.320
that it seemed she had been 
sweet-talked by a nasty male tanuki.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:13.440
Seriously, they are forever 
meddling in the most unnecessary ways.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.870
They take such good 
care of their little sister.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:28.830
You're cute when you're round, so 
keep being a Daruma for a bit.

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:30.210
Where are we off to?

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:34.130
Besides totaling my inner parlor

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.030
you lost my precious folding fan.

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:40.020
You made a promise to provide entertainment 
for the Friday Fellows, right?

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.880
I won't let you say you forgot it.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:47.110
I have no words to express my regret for 
what happened during the Fire Festival.

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:48.810
But that--

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.520
I don't need apologies.

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:55.830
We'll just eat you if we 
don't enjoy your performance.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:17.670
Do you like sukiyaki?

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:22.550
Besides tanuki hot pot, 
there's nothing in this world I don't.

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:26.320
I like tanuki hot pot better than sukiyaki.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:27.920
How whimsical.

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:31.100
Beef is infinitely tastier.

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:35.600
Your dad was boiled in a hot pot.

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:38.680
I wonder how many 
years its been since then.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:43.920
You say that like you 
weren't sitting there eating it.

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:48.860
It was right after I was 
welcomed into the Friday Fellows.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:52.530
It was the first time 
I had ever eaten tanuki.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:56.210
It was a delicious hot pot.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:05.400
Professor!

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:06.720
Hey.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:11.130
This evening's entertainment...

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:13.500
I'm Shimogamo Yasaburo.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:18.170
Jurojin and Fukurokuju will be absent.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.150
I let the restaurant know in advance.

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:25.660
Well then, since all of today's 
members are here, shall we begin?

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:36.660
The sound and smell alone are more than 
enough to put me in a beer-drinking mood.

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:40.030
Then, Ebisu, you can just 
stick to drinking beer.

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:42.010
I'll eat your share!

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:46.490
No, no, no, there's only an 
opener because of the main event.

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:49.020
Tasty meat is poison for your body.

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:53.430
The one smiling and 
laughing over there is Ebisu.

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:56.020
The big one is Bishamon.

00:11:56.670 --> 00:12:00.330
Ebisu holds a high position 
at a bank in Osaka.

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:04.300
Bishamon is the president 
of the hotel Sengyokaku.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.780
A man of letters once said,

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:10.790
"Cows eat straw, so this 
isn't beef hot pot, but straw hot pot."

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:15.290
 If it's straw then there's 
probably no cholesterol.

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:15.290
Daikoku is the young proprietor of the 
Kyoto cuisine restaurant Chitose-ya.

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:18.200
There isn't any, right Professor?

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:22.010
I wonder if cows these days even eat straw.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:24.970
Hotei is a university teacher.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:29.610
Cows these days drink beer 
while listening to Mozart.

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:29.000
There are two others, but 
they're absent today.

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:32.510
I wanted to see Jurojin...

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:33.310
So that means we're eating 
beer while drinking beer?

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.730
What kind of person is Jurojin?

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:37.770
That's like eating rice with a side of rice.

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.820
He's a shark.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:39.070
A shark?

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:40.980
You mean a card shark?

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.760
A loan shark.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.950
We're lucky Hotei is 
at the other hot pot today.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:06.290
Hotei is fine with it being raw,

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:09.560
so if you're not paying 
attention you won't get to eat.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:11.650
Brother.

00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:14.990
What do you say?

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:19.350
They don't seem to be taking this very 
seriously, sitting over there cross-legged in peace.

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:23.970
Quite so. Let us teach 
them the harshness of reality!

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:30.490
It's about time we head into 
the entertainment portion of the evening.

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:32.830
We've been waiting!

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:37.000
That dumbass.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.000
<b>Teramachi shopping district</b>

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.000
<b>Nishizaki Genemon's shop</b>

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.000
<b> Sukiyaki restaurant</b>

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:44.130
And now, presenting the secret ceremony 
passed down in the Shimogamo family since long ago

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:48.230
"The Seven Transformations Kuru Kuru Pon Pon"

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:49.760
Shall we begin?

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:56.810
Just getting started!

00:13:58.620 --> 00:13:59.630
One more!

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:02.510
And even this!

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.010
Keep going, keep going!

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:14.790
If you get too carried away, I'll eat you.

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:20.550
Thank you very much.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:27.810
Amazing! I would expect 
nothing less from a guest of Benten.

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:31.000
I have no idea what the trick could be.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.510
Are you, by any chance, a tanuki?

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:37.670
That's right, I'm a tanuki.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:39.320
Indeed, he is.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:43.980
He's a tanuki I know. Doesn't he look tasty?

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:48.450
No, it would be a waste to eat him, 
with such talent. I couldn't eat him!

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:51.570
I've taken a liking to you! You're fantastic!

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:52.980
So interesting!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.020
Come again next time!

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:03.000
Here, please eat. Keep on eating!

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:06.940
I guess I'll forgive you for tonight.

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:10.050
You mean you won't boil me in a hot pot?

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:13.440
Well I don't know about tomorrow.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:19.300
Next month's year-end 
bash is tanuki hot pot, huh.

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:22.850
As usual, we'll borrow Chitose-ya.

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:25.300
Of course, it's fine to do it at my place.

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:29.680
I doubt other restaurants 
would let you make tanuki hot pot.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:34.770
Why is it that we have to eat tanuki 
hot pot at the year-end bash, anyways?

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:37.100
I prefer beef.

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:41.670
If you talk like that you'll be expelled 
from the club. It's a rule, that's why.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:45.120
Wasn't it Tanizaki Junichiro who decided it?

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.200
Is that true?

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:51.260
I heard from Jurojin that 
Tanizaki Junichiro was a member.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:53.280
Sounds like a lie to me.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:56.870
Would Tanizaki eat <i>tanuki</i> though?

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.850
Wasn't he into eel?

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:03.510
But eel is a summer food.

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:07.450
Next up to bring a tanuki is Hotei, right?

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:11.820
Hotei, you like tanuki, don't you.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:17.980
Tanuki are cute, aren't they? How cute!

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:22.140
The way they're all short 'n stout
 is charming, don't you think?

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:25.550
Also the way their eyes look at you blankly,

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:28.330
the way their butts wiggle 
as they timidly scurry away...

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:29.830
I see.

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:35.130
That time I fell head over heels 
for a tanuki was so many years ago,

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:38.810
but that tanuki was such a cutie.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:41.880
It happened when I was 
walking alone in Kitashirakawa.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:53.230
You poor thing. You're hurt?

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:55.440
Okay, c'mere.

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:00.200
Maybe it was because her
 leg was injured and it hurt,

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:03.760
but I picked her up and carried her to my 
house and she didn't struggle or anything.

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:07.940
Then I dressed her wound, 
made some rice balls,

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:13.410
That tanuki would gobble up 
anything -- she really loved to eat.

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:15.180
Just like me!

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:19.900
She was terribly scared 
whenever it thundered.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:23.270
Hm? She was scared of... thunder?

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:28.440
Sure was. She would run 
around whimpering, poor thing.

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:34.230
On nights when it thundered, I covered her 
in a blanket and stayed with her the whole time.

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:40.180
She got better, so I 
returned her to the mountains,

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:44.460
but as she was leaving 
she actually looked at my face!

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:47.430
She kept looking back as she went!

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:51.840
Ah, Bishamon, you don't believe me, do you?

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:54.420
Because you didn't see her.

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:57.810
Because you didn't see how cute she was!

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:02.330
She understood that I had 
done her a favor by saving her.

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:00.600
Uh huh.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:03.090
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:05.310
They're clever, tanuki are.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.310
Sure, sure. Yep.

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:10.900
Ever since then I've 
been in love with tanuki.

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:13.300
That's why it's so weird!

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:17.740
Hotei, we all know have a thing for tanuki.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:22.830
But don't you happily scarf 
tanuki hot pot every year?

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.620
Isn't that bizarre?

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:30.560
Liking tanuki and eating 
tanuki are not contradictory.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:34.670
There will always be guys 
like you who eat it reluctantly,

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:37.720
but I'm always happy to.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:41.580
Eating and thinking how delicious 
it is, that's simply good manners.

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:47.260
But there's no reason to go out 
of your way to eat tanuki, is there?

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:50.940
There's plenty of other tasty things.

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:54.650
I like them so much I 
want to eat them up, yes I do.

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:58.580
I've known you for a long time, Hotei,

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:01.490
but I still don't understand you.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:06.320
Ahh, I want you to understand! 
It's love! Love! You get it, right?

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:07.200
No, I don't!

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:08.950
I don't get <i>that</i>.

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:12.810
But you know, tanuki are cute,

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:16.390
but there's someone here 
who is just as cute as them!

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:21.190
This is no good. Hotei's wasted again.

00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:23.190
I know how you feel, but control yourself!

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:24.470
Impossible! 

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:27.630
Hey, I've gotten kinda bored.

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:29.990
Let's go outside.

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.950
Hey, Benten!

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:41.440
Come back!

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:49.620
There's a huge moon out!

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:53.010
I like round things.

00:19:53.010 --> 00:19:54.330
Is that so?

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:58.170
I want the moon!

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:02.320
Hey, go get it, Yasaburo!

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:06.930
But that's absurd, 
even as a favor for you...

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:08.820
Yeah, you're a good-for-nothing.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:11.390
Can't do anything.

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:15.270
You're such a pitiful tanuki.

00:20:15.550 --> 00:20:17.730
By all means, please continue...

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:20.440
When the moon is pretty

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:24.240
I get kind of sad.

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:26.220
You're just drunk.

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:29.880
Am not, not on that little bit.

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:58.940
What are you so upset about?

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:02.830
You poor thing, 
you'll be eaten by me.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:05.910
But couldn't you just not eat me?

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:10.410
But, at some point I'm 
definitely going to eat you up.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:13.990
I have issues with the fact that 
you can say "I'll eat you up" so easily.

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:16.930
It's a matter of life or death for me.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.790
I just like you so 
much I wanna eat you up.

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:22.920
But if you eat the thing you like,

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:27.050
then the thing you like will be gone!

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:31.090
What would you expect? You're so spoiled.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:37.650
Despite my unwillingness, I gathered
 around a delicious sukiyaki hot pot

00:21:37.870 --> 00:21:42.150
with the Friday Fellows, the guys 
responsible for the death of our dad.

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:48.520
That night Benten and 
I said a toast to the moon.

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:57.980
Then as she drank the cocktail in her hand, 
for some reason she murmured, "So sad, so sad."

00:23:30.790 --> 00:23:34.030
Yodogawa here. It's 
really autumn now, huh.

00:23:34.030 --> 00:23:36.390
Clear skies and a healthy 
appetite in the fall.

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:38.300
Hm? It's the middle of summer?

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Taking in Fall Colors</b>

00:23:38.300 --> 00:23:39.930
Oh.
